From 27d40ed2daac0ab97797eb633991518586027616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:36:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] usb: dwc3: force a 32-bit DMA mask on SM8150

The controller advertises a 64-bit address width, so the driver asks for a
64-bit mask.  On SM8150 that lets the ep0 TRB land below the start of DRAM
(0x80000000) and the first controller DMA wedges the NoC.

Restrict coherent allocations to the low 4 GiB, which is the layout the stock
firmware uses.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
index ee56148eb..f6b1ecdd1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2276,9 +2276,15 @@ int dwc3_core_probe(const struct dwc3_probe_data *data)
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, dwc);
 	dwc3_cache_hwparams(dwc);
 
-	if (!dev_is_pci(dwc->sysdev) &&
-	    DWC3_GHWPARAMS0_AWIDTH(dwc->hwparams.hwparams0) == 64) {
-		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	/*
+	 * The controller advertises a 64-bit address width, so upstream asks for a
+	 * 64-bit mask.  On SM8150 that lets the ep0 TRB land below the start of DRAM
+	 * (0x80000000) and the first controller DMA wedges the NoC.  Restricting
+	 * coherent allocations to the low 4 GiB keeps them inside DRAM, which is the
+	 * layout the stock firmware uses.
+	 */
+	if (!dev_is_pci(dwc->sysdev)) {
+		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_disable_clks;
 	}
